## Test Anti-Pattern Audit — `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

**Summary: 10 tests, 13 findings (6 Critical · 1 High · 1 Medium · 1 Low)**

This suite is a textbook **coverage-touching** suite. Every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called, giving 95%+ coverage, but almost nothing is actually verified. A bug in any method would not cause a test failure.

---

### 🔴 Critical — Tests giving false confidence

#### 1. Coverage-Touching Pattern (systemic)
**Lines 6–89 (entire class)**
All 10 tests methodically call every public method in declaration order, with names like `*_Works`, and either have **no assertion at all** or only a trivial `Assert.IsNotNull` that proves nothing about correctness. This is the #1 reason bugs reach production despite 95% coverage.

---

#### 2. No Assertions — 4 tests that verify nothing

| Test (line) | What's untested |
|---|---|
| `AddProduct_Works` (17) | Product actually persisted? |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` (32) | Price actually changed? |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` (39) | Product actually removed? |
| `GetProductCount_Works` (64) | Count correct? |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (69) | Prices actually discounted? |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` (85) | Products actually imported? |

**Fix — `AddProduct_Works` (example, apply pattern to all):**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_StoresProductRetrievableBySku()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);

    var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved?.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved?.Price);
}
```

**Fix — `UpdatePrice_Works`:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_ChangesStoredPrice()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);

    var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated?.Price);
}
```

**Fix — `RemoveProduct_Works`:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void RemoveProduct_MakesProductUnretrievable()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");

    Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
}
```

**Fix — `GetProductCount_Works`:**
